# QuantumVault's own detection rules, reference tables, and report/label text
# contain cryptographic algorithm NAMES as match patterns and human-readable
# strings — they are rule definitions, not cryptographic usage. Exclude them
# from a self-scan so the inventory reflects what the product actually uses
# (which is: no quantum-vulnerable crypto). Test directories and sample-target/
# are already skipped by default.
server/src/discovery/patterns.ts
server/src/discovery/cryptoRef.ts
server/src/discovery/context.ts
# x509.ts is the DER certificate READER: its OID tables and algorithm-name
# vocabulary (RSA/ECDSA/ML-DSA OIDs, curve names) are detection reference data,
# not cryptographic usage — same precedent as patterns.ts / cryptoRef.ts.
server/src/discovery/x509.ts
server/src/compliance/reporter.ts
server/src/report/assessment.ts
server/src/cli.ts
# The benchmark suite vendors NO product crypto — it holds detection-rule text,
# per-finding labels for OTHER repos, and corpora fetched at runtime. Not part of
# the product's own cryptographic posture.
bench
